  "query_preview": "..Today and Thursday...High pressure remains in control\nover Arizona over the next couple of days. Near-normal temperatures\nand dry conditions look to prevail as a result, along with light \nwinds.\n\nFriday and Saturday...A weakening low ejects off the Pacific on \nFriday into southern California. Moisture advection looks to \nincrease over the region, leading to showers developing late Friday \nacross central Arizona.\n\nA secondary, stronger trough looks to set in over much of the west \non Saturday. With the area already primed from the earlier low, a \nmore widespread round of showers looks likely. With the upper-level \njet largely in place across far northern Arizona, the greatest \nchances for precipitation look to be focused along the higher terrain \nnear the Arizona-Utah border. However, given the lack of robust \nforcing, overall QPF amounts look to be on the lighter side. Much of \nthe guidance seems to favor around 0.30-0.60 inches across the \nhigher terrain (especially north) and only a few hundredths to a \ncouple tenths possible in the lower elevations.\n\n700 mb temperatures remain fairly warm around 0C to -2C, which \nshould keep snow levels around 8000-9000 feet. Thus, the most likely \nareas will to see any snowfall will be across only the highest \nelevations. Some snow may mix in late Saturday down to around 7000 \nfeet, however accumulations look to be unlikely.\n\nGusty southwest winds also look to be likely on Saturday. As of now, \nthe strongest gusts look to mainly be in the 35-45 mph and mainly \ndownwind of the Mogollon Rim, across the Little Colorado River \nValley and into portions of Navajo Nation. A Wind Advisory may be \nneeded for these areas Saturday afternoon.\n\nSunday through Tuesday...High pressure briefly builds back into \nArizona for the start of the week, ushering in a return of milder \ntemperatures and drier conditions. This looks to be short-lived \nhowever, as a more potent low looks to move into the region on \nTuesday. Confidence remains low at this point however, as model \nsolutions still differ on the exact track and depth of the low at \nthis point. Nevertheless, unsettled weather looks to set in by the \nmiddle of next week.",
